{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/(z^2 - 1):\n    z = -1  order 1, residue -1/2\n    z = 1  order 1, residue 1/2\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "poles", "ucas": "poles 1/(z^2-1)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "poles", "var": "z", "poles": [{"at": "-1", "order": 1, "residue": "-1/2"}, {"at": "1", "order": 1, "residue": "1/2"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/(z^2 - 1):\n    z = -1  order 1, residue -1/2\n    z = 1  order 1, residue 1/2\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of log(z)/(z - 1) at z = 1:\n  = 0\n  log(z)/(z - 1) is regular there (or the singularity is removable): the residue is 0\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of log(z)/(z - 1) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "residue", "ucas": "residue log(z)/(z-1) at 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "residue", "var": "z", "at": "1", "found": true, "residue": "0", "re": 0, "im": 0, "singularity": "regular"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "circle_integrals", "points": 1024, "passed": true, "text": "radius 0.01 and 0.005 agree"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of log(z)/(z - 1) at z = 1:\n  = 0\n  log(z)/(z - 1) is regular there (or the singularity is removable): the residue is 0\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of log(z)/(z - 1) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nd/dz log(z) = 1/z\n  the complex derivative: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  holomorphic except at log (the branch cuts of the principal values)\n  check: equals the difference quotient at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 4e-10)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "diff", "ucas": "diff log(z) z", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "diff", "var": "z", "holomorphic": true, "derivative": "1/z", "entire": false, "except": "log (the branch cuts of the principal values)"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "cauchy_riemann", "points": 64, "max_diff": 2.4456899688454526e-10, "passed": true, "text": "df/dx = df/(i dy) at sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2]"}, {"kind": "difference_quotient", "points": 64, "max_diff": 3.7344814621730633e-10, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nd/dz log(z) = 1/z\n  the complex derivative: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  holomorphic except at log (the branch cuts of the principal values)\n  check: equals the difference quotient at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 4e-10)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nd/dz sqrt(z) = 1/(2sqrt(z))\n  the complex derivative: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  holomorphic except at sqrt (the branch cuts of the principal values)\n  check: equals the difference quotient at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 1e-10)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "diff", "ucas": "diff sqrt(z) z", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "diff", "var": "z", "holomorphic": true, "derivative": "1/(2sqrt(z))", "entire": false, "except": "sqrt (the branch cuts of the principal values)"}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "cauchy_riemann", "points": 64, "max_diff": 9.045418441299049e-11, "passed": true, "text": "df/dx = df/(i dy) at sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2]"}, {"kind": "difference_quotient", "points": 64, "max_diff": 1.266415250876473e-10, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nd/dz sqrt(z) = 1/(2sqrt(z))\n  the complex derivative: the Cauchy-Riemann equations hold at 64 sample points of [-2, 2] x [-2, 2] (df/dx = df/(i dy))\n  holomorphic except at sqrt (the branch cuts of the principal values)\n  check: equals the difference quotient at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 1e-10)\n"}, "isError": false}}
